# Citation metadata: GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" box from this file, and
# Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. Update `version` and `date-released`
# at every release. `doi` is the Zenodo concept DOI ("Cite all versions"), the same for every version.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyATCLI in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PyATCLI: analysis library, engine and command line for PyAT"
type: software
version: "2026.11.5"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23994241"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PyATCLI"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/PyATCLI/"
url: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PyATCLI"
abstract: >-
  The analysis library, engine and command line behind PyAT (Python Analysis Tool): fibre-photometry
  (TDT) motion and photobleaching correction, dF/F, event-locked z-score PETH, peak finding,
  AUC, FFT, curve fitting and group (mixed-model) statistics, plus loaders for Oxysoft NIRS, generic
  tabular data and Terranova EFNMR files, and a provenance record for every result so it can be
  reproduced. It draws nothing and contains no GUI code. Called PhysicsLibrary (PyPI:
  ZaksPhysicsLibrary) before it became PyATCLI.
keywords:
  - fibre photometry
  - neuroscience
  - signal processing
  - dF/F
  - PETH
authors:
  - family-names: "Grand Maison"
    given-names: "Zakary"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-3946-0616"
    affiliation: "Concordia University"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
